{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat -n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/safepoint.cljc; cat -n src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.python.antlr.safepoint\n     2\t  \"The Python hook prelude for `yang.safepoint` (Architect safepoint\n     3\t   design, slice 1: signals; slice 2: recursion). Universal AST, like the\n     4\t   base prelude; the stage only places `(py.sp/loop)`, `(py.sp/call)` and\n     5\t   `(py.sp/return body)`, and what they mean is written here.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Signals. The composition hands the task a signal stream, a sealed\n     8\t   reference in the store under `signals-key`; a host adapter appends one\n     9\t   plain value per delivered signal. Each hook reads it with `stream/poll!`,\n    10\t   which answers `:dao.stream/blocked` rather than parking, so a program\n    11\t   with no signal pending never waits at a safepoint. On a signal (or a\n    12\t   gap: values were lost, so at least one arrived) the registered Python\n    13\t   handler is called with the signal and None, as CPython calls\n    14\t   `handler(signum, frame)`; with none registered, `KeyboardInterrupt` is\n    15\t   raised there, through `py/raise`: an explicit continuation invoke at an\n    16\t   explicit program point. Delivery is not journalled (owner decision 8).\n    17\t\n    18\t   Recursion (slice 2). Depth measures the current continuation: it is\n    19\t   `:base` plus `:depth` of the base prelude's dynamic-context record\n    20\t   `py.rt/ctx`, the one cell that also holds the handler stack (`:base` is\n    21\t   0 outside generators; each crossing into a generator sets it to the\n    22\t   resumer's absolute depth plus one). `py.sp/call`, at the head of every\n    23\t   Python function body, increments `:depth` and raises `RecursionError`\n    24\t   through `py/raise` when the absolute depth would exceed the limit;\n    25\t   `py.sp/return`, which the stage applies to the body's value, decrements\n    26\t   it on normal exit. An escape (an exception caught above, a `return`\n    27\t   through `finally`) runs no exit hook: it restores the record its\n    28\t   capture point saved, current `:base` kept, so the depth is restored,\n    29\t   never decremented. The limit counts Python function frames: with limit\n    30\t   n, n nested calls run and the next raises. It lives in the cell\n    31\t   `py.sp/limit`, 1000 by default, outside the escape-restored record, so\n    32\t   a change survives escapes; `py.sp/set-recursion-limit!` sets it as\n    33\t   `sys.setrecursionlimit` would (the Python surface is not reachable yet:\n    34\t   the lowering refuses `import`).\n    35\t\n    36\t   Load order. The base prelude is bundled into every program tree, so the\n    37\t   hook prelude loads before it and may not touch a base definition while\n    38\t   loading: it allocates only cells and a cursor. `KeyboardInterrupt`,\n    39\t   `RecursionError` and `py.rt/ctx` are base-prelude definitions; the\n    40\t   hooks name them only inside their bodies, so the names resolve when a\n    41\t   hook runs, after the base prelude has loaded. Every key this prelude\n    42\t   defines is in `py.sp`.\"\n    43\t  (:require\n    44\t    [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]))\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(def profile\n    48\t  \"The `yang.safepoint` profile this prelude implements: site kind -> hook.\"\n    49\t  {:loop 'py.sp/loop, :call 'py.sp/call, :return 'py.sp/return})\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(def default-recursion-limit\n    53\t  \"CPython's default `sys.getrecursionlimit()`.\"\n    54\t  1000)\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t(def signals-key\n    58\t  \"The store key the composition binds the signal stream's reference to.\"\n    59\t  'py.sp/signals)\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(def host-names\n    63\t  \"Module exports this prelude calls: the cell module, and the stream\n    64\t   module's `cursor` and `poll!`.\"\n    65\t  '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! stream/cursor stream/poll!})\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(def ^:private function-definitions\n    69\t  '[[py.sp/set-handler! (fn [h] (cell/set! py.sp/handler h))]\n    70\t    [py.sp/deliver\n    71\t     (fn [sig]\n    72\t       (let [h (cell/get py.sp/handler)]\n    73\t         (if (= h :py/None)\n    74\t           (py/raise (py/call py.b/KeyboardInterrupt []))\n    75\t           (do (py/call h (py/conj (py/conj [] sig) :py/None))\n    76\t               :py/None))))]\n    77\t    [py.sp/poll\n    78\t     (fn []\n    79\t       (let [s (stream/poll! py.sp/cursor)]\n    80\t         (if (= s :dao.stream/blocked)\n    81\t           :py/None\n    82\t           (if (nil? s) :py/None (py.sp/deliver s)))))]\n    83\t    [py.sp/enter\n    84\t     (fn []\n    85\t       (let [c (cell/get py.rt/ctx)\n    86\t             d (+ 1 (get c :depth))]\n    87\t         (if (< (cell/get py.sp/limit) (+ (get c :base) d))\n    88\t           (py/raise-new py.b/RecursionError\n    89\t                         {:py/str \"maximum recursion depth exceeded\"})\n    90\t           (cell/set! py.rt/ctx (assoc c :depth d)))))]\n    91\t    [py.sp/loop (fn [] (py.sp/poll))]\n    92\t    [py.sp/call (fn [] (do (py.sp/poll) (py.sp/enter)))]\n    93\t    [py.sp/return\n    94\t     (fn [v]\n    95\t       (let [c (cell/get py.rt/ctx)]\n    96\t         (do (cell/set! py.rt/ctx (assoc c :depth (- (get c :depth) 1)))\n    97\t             v)))]\n    98\t    [py.sp/recursion-limit (fn [] (cell/get py.sp/limit))]\n    99\t    [py.sp/set-recursion-limit!\n   100\t     ;; sys.setrecursionlimit: an int (bool included), at least 1, and above\n   101\t     ;; the current absolute depth; a refused limit leaves the old one\n   102\t     (fn [n]\n   103\t       (if (py/int? n)\n   104\t         (if (< (py/num n) 1)\n   105\t           (py/raise-new py.b/ValueError\n   106\t                         {:py/str \"recursion limit must be greater or equal than 1\"})\n   107\t           (if (<= (py/num n) (py/abs-depth (cell/get py.rt/ctx)))\n   108\t             (py/raise-new py.b/RecursionError\n   109\t                           {:py/str \"cannot set the recursion limit: the limit is too low\"})\n   110\t             (do (cell/set! py.sp/limit (py/num n)) :py/None)))\n   111\t         (py/type-error {:py/str \"an integer is required\"})))]])\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(def ^:private state-definitions\n   115\t  [['py.sp/handler '(cell/new :py/None)]\n   116\t   ['py.sp/limit (list 'cell/new default-recursion-limit)]\n   117\t   ['py.sp/cursor '(stream/cursor py.sp/signals)]])\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn- definitions->uast\n   121\t  [defs]\n   122\t  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(def uast\n   126\t  \"The hook prelude: functions, then its cells and the signal cursor.\"\n   127\t  (u/mark-tails (u/then (definitions->uast function-definitions)\n   128\t                        (definitions->uast state-definitions))))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(def noop-uast\n   132\t  \"Hooks that do nothing: the derived program under them is the naive one.\"\n   133\t  (u/mark-tails (definitions->uast '[[py.sp/loop (fn [] :py/None)]\n   134\t                                     [py.sp/call (fn [] :py/None)]\n   135\t                                     [py.sp/return (fn [v] v)]])))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn program\n   139\t  \"The derived run's tree: `hooks` (a hook prelude), then the derived\n   140\t   program `ast`.\"\n   141\t  [hooks ast]\n   142\t  (u/then hooks ast))\n     1\t(ns yang.safepoint\n     2\t  \"The safepoint stage (Architect safepoint-interpreter design, slice 1): a\n     3\t   pure rewrite of a canonical program tree `A` into a derived tree `A'` that\n     4\t   applies a hook at every frontend-marked site the profile maps.\n     5\t   Language-neutral: it knows the Universal AST row grammar and the\n     6\t   frontend-metadata side table, nothing about any guest language. The hooks'\n     7\t   meaning lives in a per-language hook prelude; the evaluator never learns\n     8\t   what a safepoint is.\n     9\t\n    10\t   - A site is a `:lambda` occurrence the frontend marked with `:yang/site`\n    11\t     metadata, which projection puts in the side table as\n    12\t     `[origin root path :yang/site kind]`. A profile `{kind hook-symbol}`\n    13\t     selects sites; a kind it omits is not inserted.\n    14\t   - Insertion prefixes the site's body with an ordinary `:application` of\n    15\t     the hook, sequenced through a lambda whose one binder is `binder`, in a\n    16\t     reserved namespace: no new tag, no gensym counter. An exit kind\n    17\t     (`exit-kinds`: `:return` at `:call` sites) wraps the body instead: its\n    18\t     hook is applied to the body's value, so it runs on normal exit only.\n    19\t   - Every tail mark is stripped and recomputed over the whole derived tree\n    20\t     (`yang.tails`): a wrapped body's old tail calls would otherwise skip\n    21\t     its wrapper. With no site selected `A'` is `A`, row for row.\n    22\t   - `A` is never modified. Names, the ledger and publication refer to it;\n    23\t     the link is a `:derive` record with input `A`, output `A'`, function\n    24\t     `function`, and a profile pinning the hook map and the address of the\n    25\t     sorted site set. Insertion is deterministic, so a repeat writes the\n    26\t     same record.\n    27\t   - `A'` leaves on the stage's own medium in a projected envelope whose\n    28\t     batch token is the record's address, so its occurrence origin is an\n    29\t     ordinary `[:source medium' token 0]`. No side table is copied: an `A'`\n    30\t     node's facts are a join back to `A` through the site set.\"\n    31\t  (:require\n    32\t    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    33\t    [yang.stage :as stage]\n    34\t    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    35\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\t(def binder\n    39\t  \"The parameter of every inserted sequencing lambda.\"\n    40\t  'yang.safepoint/_)\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(def function\n    44\t  \"The `:yin.ledger/function` of a safepoint derivation.\"\n    45\t  :yang.safepoint/insert)\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(def site-key\n    49\t  \"The frontend-metadata key a site mark travels under.\"\n    50\t  :yang/site)\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn sites\n    54\t  \"`{path kind}` of every site marked in the frontend-metadata relation\n    55\t   `metadata` at occurrence `origin` of tree `root`.\"\n    56\t  [metadata origin root]\n    57\t  (into {}\n    58\t        (keep (fn [[o r path k v]]\n    59\t                (when (and (= o origin) (= r root) (= k site-key))\n    60\t                  [path v])))\n    61\t        metadata))\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(defn site-set\n    65\t  \"The selected sites as a sorted vector of `[path kind]`, in an order every\n    66\t   host computes alike.\"\n    67\t  [selected]\n    68\t  (vec (sort-by pr-str (map vec selected))))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(def exit-kinds\n    72\t  \"Exit kind -> the entry kind whose sites it wraps. An exit hook is applied\n    73\t   to the value of the site's body, so it runs after a normal exit and its\n    74\t   answer is the body's value; an escape out of the body skips it.\"\n    75\t  {:return :call})\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn- site-hooks\n    79\t  \"`{:enter hook :exit hook}` (either absent) for a site of `kind` under\n    80\t   `profile`.\"\n    81\t  [profile kind]\n    82\t  (let [exit (some (fn [[x entry]] (when (= entry kind) (get profile x)))\n    83\t                   exit-kinds)]\n    84\t    (cond-> {}\n    85\t      (get profile kind) (assoc :enter (get profile kind))\n    86\t      exit (assoc :exit exit))))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- hook-application\n    90\t  [hook operands]\n    91\t  {:type :application,\n    92\t   :operator {:type :variable, :name hook},\n    93\t   :operands operands})\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn- prefix-hook\n    97\t  \"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied before its body runs.\"\n    98\t  [node hook]\n    99\t  (assoc node\n   100\t         :body {:type :application,\n   101\t                :operator {:type :lambda, :params [binder], :body (:body node)},\n   102\t                :operands [(hook-application hook [])]}))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(defn- wrap-hook\n   106\t  \"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied to its body's value.\"\n   107\t  [node hook]\n   108\t  (assoc node :body (hook-application hook [(:body node)])))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(defn- rewrite\n   112\t  \"The map AST `ast` with each `{path {:enter h :exit h}}` site's exit hook\n   113\t   wrapped around its body and its entry hook prefixed. Throws when a site\n   114\t   names no node, or a node that is not a lambda.\"\n   115\t  [ast hooks]\n   116\t  (let [seen (volatile! #{})]\n   117\t    (letfn [(walk\n   118\t              [node path]\n   119\t              (let [slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node))\n   120\t                    node (reduce\n   121\t                           (fn [n [j [field kind]]]\n   122\t                             (let [pos (+ j 2)]\n   123\t                               (case kind\n   124\t                                 :node (update n field walk (conj path pos))\n   125\t                                 :nodes (update n field\n   126\t                                                (fn [children]\n   127\t                                                  (vec (map-indexed\n   128\t                                                         (fn [i child]\n   129\t                                                           (walk child (conj path [pos i])))\n   130\t                                                         children))))\n   131\t                                 n)))\n   132\t                           node\n   133\t                           (map-indexed vector slots))]\n   134\t                (if-let [{:keys [enter exit]} (get hooks path)]\n   135\t                  (do (when-not (= :lambda (:type node))\n   136\t                        (throw (ex-info \"Safepoint site is not a lambda\"\n   137\t                                        {:rule :site-not-lambda, :path path,\n   138\t                                         :type (:type node)})))\n   139\t                      (vswap! seen conj path)\n   140\t                      (cond-> node\n   141\t                        exit (wrap-hook exit)\n   142\t                        enter (prefix-hook enter)))\n   143\t                  node)))]\n   144\t      (let [out (walk ast [])\n   145\t            missing (remove @seen (keys hooks))]\n   146\t        (when (seq missing)\n   147\t          (throw (ex-info \"Safepoint site names no node\"\n   148\t                          {:rule :site-missing, :paths (vec (sort-by pr-str missing))})))\n   149\t        out))))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn insert\n   153\t  \"Pure: the canonical row set `tree` (`{:root id :rows {id row}}`) with\n   154\t   each of `sites` (`{path kind}`) that `profile` (`{kind hook}`) maps a\n   155\t   hook to, by its kind or by an exit kind of it, rewritten: the entry hook\n   156\t   prefixed, the exit hook wrapped around the body. Returns\n   157\t   `{:tree A' :sites selected}`. With nothing selected `A'` is `tree`\n   158\t   itself.\"\n   159\t  [tree sites profile]\n   160\t  (let [hooks (into {}\n   161\t                    (keep (fn [[path kind]]\n   162\t                            (let [h (site-hooks profile kind)]\n   163\t                              (when (seq h) [path h]))))\n   164\t                    sites)\n   165\t        selected (into {} (filter (fn [[path _]] (contains? hooks path))) sites)]\n   166\t    {:tree (if (empty? hooks)\n   167\t             tree\n   168\t             (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode\n   169\t               (tails/remark-tails\n   170\t                 (rewrite (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast tree) hooks))))\n   171\t     :sites selected}))\n   172\t\n   173\t\n   174\t(defn derive-record\n   175\t  \"The `:derive` record linking canonical root `input` to derived root\n   176\t   `output`: function `function`, profile pinning the hook map and the\n   177\t   address of the sorted site set.\"\n   178\t  [input output profile selected]\n   179\t  {:yin.ledger/op :derive,\n   180\t   :yin.ledger/input input,\n   181\t   :yin.ledger/output output,\n   182\t   :yin.ledger/function function,\n   183\t   :yin.ledger/profile {:yang.safepoint/hooks profile,\n   184\t                        :yang.safepoint/sites (jing/segment-key\n   185\t                                                (site-set selected))}})\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t(defn derive-envelope\n   189\t  \"One projected envelope from the row medium to the derived one:\n   190\t   `{:envelope e' :record r :record-address a}`. The run member of the input\n   191\t   is `A`; `e'` carries `A'` alone, on `medium`, with token `a`.\"\n   192\t  [envelope profile medium]\n   193\t  (let [{:yin/keys [source-medium batch-token batch root frontend-metadata]}\n   194\t        envelope\n   195\t        tree (nth batch root)\n   196\t        origin (vm/source-origin source-medium batch-token root)\n   197\t        {derived :tree selected :sites}\n   198\t        (insert tree (sites frontend-metadata origin (:root tree)) profile)\n   199\t        record (derive-record (:root tree) (:root derived) profile selected)\n   200\t        address (jing/segment-key record)]\n   201\t    (vm/source-origin medium address 0)\n   202\t    {:envelope {:yin/source-medium medium,\n   203\t                :yin/batch-token address,\n   204\t                :yin/batch [derived],\n   205\t                :yin/root 0,\n   206\t                :yin/source-positions [],\n   207\t                :yin/frontend-metadata [],\n   208\t                :yin/entity-occurrences []},\n   209\t     :record record,\n   210\t     :record-address address}))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t(defn transform\n   214\t  \"The stage's transform over projected envelopes: `A'` on port `:program`,\n   215\t   its `:derive` record on port `:ledger`. State is `{:profile p :medium m}`\n   216\t   and never changes.\"\n   217\t  [{:keys [profile medium], :as state} envelope]\n   218\t  (let [{:keys [envelope record]} (derive-envelope envelope profile medium)]\n   219\t    [state [[:program envelope] [:ledger record]]]))\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t(defn open-stage\n   223\t  \"A safepoint stage reading projected envelopes from `rows`, writing derived\n   224\t   envelopes to `program` (logical identity `medium`) and records to\n   225\t   `ledger`.\"\n   226\t  [rows program ledger profile medium]\n   227\t  (stage/open rows\n   228\t              {:program program, :ledger ledger}\n   229\t              {:profile profile, :medium medium}))\n   230\t\n   231\t\n   232\t(defn step-stage\n   233\t  [s]\n   234\t  (stage/step s transform))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
